  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Protection and Mixed Solutions Dzakela Camp (MWI306)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In the year 2023, Plan International Malawi will operate under the four thematic areas of SGBV, Child Protection, Human Rights and Distribution of food and non-food items with an overall objective of providing effective and efficient protection services to refugees and asylum seekers in Dzaleka with particular focus on vulnerable groups such as unaccompanied and separated minors, adolescent girls and young women and people living with disabilities. Specifically, the project will achieve the following objectives:_x000d_
_x000d_
a)	 Persons of concern have optimal access to sexual and reproductive health and HIV services.  _x000d_
b)	Persons of concern have sufficient basic and domestic items._x000d_
c)	Services for people with specific needs provided and strengthened._x000d_
d)	Shelter and infrastructure established, improved and maintained. _x000d_
e)	Community mobilization strengthened and expanded _x000d_
f)	Civil registration and status documentation strengthened. _x000d_
g)	Public attitudes towards persons of concern improved._x000d_
h)	Operational management, coordination and support strengthened and optimized._x000d_
i)	Protection of children strengthened._x000d_
j)	Risk of SGBV is reduced and quality of response improved. _x000d_
k)	Risks related to detention reduced and freedom of movement increased. _x000d_
	_x000d_
The project will target refugees and asylum seekers in Dzaleka refugee camp, Dowa District and those living in urban settings. The project will target girls and boys, youth and the adult population. Persons with special needs such as the elderly, unaccompanied and separated minors, people with chronic illnesses and people living with disability will be given special consideration and targeting under the Gender, Age and Diversity approach.</narrative>
  </description>
